  "remaining_integration_work": [
    "Version the guardian so cgroup-lease and release-descriptor ownership transfer is unambiguous on every early failure; the frozen v1 order can otherwise leave the caller unable to distinguish a leak from a double retirement.",
    "Implement the controller-owned process topology: dedicated broker spawn, exact inherited-descriptor closure matrix, worker and guardian launch order, trusted single-writer release topology, report consumption, ledger callbacks, pidfd termination and parent-side broker and worker reap.",
    "Bind the controller into the frozen full-size bootstrap, dispatcher and lifecycle closure without weakening host, input, source, cgroup, authority, core-dump, mapping or resource-envelope gates.",
    "Authenticate the successor source closure and run a separately authorized bounded Linux native qualification before any real checkpoint payload read or import.",
    "Only after native qualification, re-run the unchanged host, input, resource and real-import admission gates."
  ],
